// Practice quiz: An integration test
// Minimum release, November 2026: author-checked, no independent review. Formative, low-stakes retention practice. Titles name the objective id each item practises.

$CATEGORY: spring-boot/integration-and-observability/an-integration-test

::o1 what loads::What does @SpringBootTest load by default? {
=The full application context#Correct. All your beans are real unless replaced.
~Only controllers#Not quite. That is the web slice.
~Only repositories#Not quite. That is the JPA slice.
~Nothing from Spring#Not quite. It does load Spring.
}

::o1 mockmvc::How do you get MockMvc in a @SpringBootTest? {
=Add @AutoConfigureMockMvc#Correct. It supplies a MockMvc bean.
~Create it with new#Not quite. That skips the configuration.
~Add @Bean to the test method#Not quite. That does not supply it.
~It is always there with no annotation#Not quite. It needs the annotation.
}

::o2 choose JPA::Which annotation best checks a repository query? {
=@DataJpaTest#Correct. It loads the persistence layer.
~@WebMvcTest#Not quite. It does not load repositories.
~@RestController#Not quite. That is not a test annotation.
~@SpringBootApplication#Not quite. That is for the app itself.
}

::o2 choose web::Which annotation best checks a validation error response? {
=@WebMvcTest#Correct. Only the web layer is involved.
~@DataJpaTest#Not quite. It does not load controllers.
~@SpringBootTest always#Not quite. That is heavier than needed.
~@Entity#Not quite. That is not a test annotation.
}

::o3 independence::What makes integration tests independent? {
=Each test sets up its own known data state#Correct. Then order does not matter.
~Running them in alphabetical order#Not quite. That hides coupling.
~Sharing rows between tests#Not quite. That is the cause of the problem.
~Removing assertions#Not quite. That removes the tests.
}

